{
  "slug": "artist:hardfloor",
  "name": "Hardfloor",
  "editorial_article": "German duo Hardfloor, comprised of Oliver Bondzio and Ramon Zenker, emerged in 1991 from Cologne to become leaders of the acid house sound. Their reputation rests on their mastery of the Roland TB-303, often utilizing up to six of these bass synthesizers simultaneously in their studio work. The duo gained mainstream attention with the 1992 hit \"Hardtrance Acperience,\" a track that Feargal Sharkey later highlighted as one of his 'Inheritance Tracks' on BBC Radio 4. Their reach extends to high-profile remix work, including versions of New Order's \"Blue Monday\" in 1995, Mory Kante's \"Yé ké yé ké,\" and Depeche Mode's \"It's No Good.\" Beyond their core output on the Harthouse label, they explore chillout and lounge genres under the pseudonym Da Damn Phreak Noize Phunk.",
